      "in_small_groups_students_practice_the_": "In small groups, students practice the mimic octopus poses: lionfish, sea snake, flatfish, jellyfish. Capture in photos or video.",
      "in_some_mediterranean_coastal_communit": "In some Mediterranean coastal communities, octopus has been a dietary staple for thousands of years — with associated TRADITIONAL fisheries knowledge that predates scientific management.",
      "in_some_species_females_are_larger_tha": "In some species, females are larger than males by 10x. Argonaut females reach 10 cm; males are 1 cm. The hectocotylus + sperm packet is the only male contribution.",
      "in_the_absence_of_predators_cephalopod": "In the absence of predators, cephalopod populations can quickly destabilize prey populations. Marine \"trophic cascades\" through cephalopods are emerging research.",
      "in_the_great_barrier_reef_130_coral_sp": "In the Great Barrier Reef, ~130 coral species spawn synchronously over 2-3 nights each November. They release gametes en masse on the same lunar cue — a strategy called \"predator satiation\" that protects most gametes by overwhelming predator capacity.",
      "in_the_hawaiian_bobtail_squid_output_i": "In the Hawaiian bobtail squid, output is controlled by varying ",
      "in_the_last_15_years_cephalopods_have_": "In the last 15 years, cephalopods have moved from \"obscure invertebrates\" to \"central figures in the philosophy of mind + the animal-welfare movement.\" A few books, a few films, a few legal documents, and a handful of celebrity individual octopuses changed how mainstream culture thinks about non-human minds.",
      "in_the_wild_an_octopus_eats_roughly_it": "In the wild, an octopus eats roughly its body mass per week. A 500 g octopus consumes ~30 crabs in seven days — and selects the largest crabs available, leaving smaller juveniles to grow.",
      "in_total_darkness_octopus_skin_chromat": "In total darkness, octopus skin chromatophores still respond to LOCAL light signals via skin opsins — they're always \"on\" even when eyes are closed.",
