      "squid_axons_are_large_enough_1_mm_diam": "Squid axons are large enough (1 mm diameter) that early electrophysiologists could insert microelectrodes by HAND. This was crucial for Hodgkin & Huxley's Nobel-Prize-winning work.",
      "squid_axons_remain_the_foundation_of_n": "Squid axons remain the foundation of neuroscience education. Many medical schools still use squid axon preparations to teach the action potential.",
      "squid_like_cephalopods_with_an_interna": "Squid-like cephalopods with an internal \"guard\" — a rocket-shaped piece of calcite that fossilizes well. They had 10 arms (vs squid's 10 = 8 + 2 tentacles) and hooklets instead of suckers. Extremely abundant in Jurassic/Cretaceous oceans.",
      "squid_mantle_sliced_into_rings_battere": "Squid mantle sliced into rings, battered, deep-fried. Italian, Greek, and Spanish coastal cuisines all have versions. Global staple of seafood restaurants.",
