      "the_thing_biologists_love_about_this_o": "🤯 The thing biologists love about this one",
      "the_three_skin_layers": "🔬 The three skin layers",
      "the_uk_animal_welfare_act_2022_added_c": "The UK Animal Welfare Act 2022 added cephalopods to its sentience list — recognizing them as conscious + capable of suffering.",
      "the_use_of_background_matching_vs_masq": "The use of background matching vs. masquerade for camouflage in cuttlefish Sepia officinalis",
      "the_vertebrate_derived_methods_work_bu": "The vertebrate-derived methods work, but their results are often mixed — because they're measuring traits that may not be cephalopod-native. The mirror test's ambiguity is a feature: it tells us cephalopods don't self-recognize the way primates do, but doesn't tell us whether they self-recognize a different way.",
      "the_vertical_lobe_of_cephalopods_an_at": "The vertical lobe of cephalopods: an attractive brain structure for understanding the evolution of advanced learning and memory",
      "the_visual_attack_of_the_cuttlefish_se": "The visual attack of the cuttlefish, Sepia officinalis",
      "the_welfare_movement_ongoing_policy": "The welfare movement + ongoing policy",
      "the_world_s_largest_invertebrate_is_th": "The world's largest invertebrate is the colossal squid — Mesonychoteuthis hamiltoni — with documented specimens up to 14 m long, including the longest known animal eyes (27 cm diameter).",
      "the_world_s_largest_octopus_arm_span_o": "The world's largest octopus — arm-span over 7 m + body mass over 50 kg have been documented. Lives along the cold Pacific coast from California to Japan. Heavily studied due to its size + tractability in captivity.",
      "the_zone_exposed_at_low_tide_submerged": "The zone exposed at low tide + submerged at high tide. Subject to extreme daily variation in temperature, salinity, oxygen, and predator pressure.",
      "their_decline_is_independent_of_human_": "Their decline is independent of human activity",
      "their_evolutionary_history_is_one_of_r": ". Their evolutionary history is one of repeated radiation + extinction + recovery, with the final survivors being the lineages we see today.",
      "their_main_competitors_are_being_fishe": " (their main competitors are being fished out); (3) ",
      "their_short_life_cycles_mean_populatio": "Their short life cycles mean populations respond rapidly (within 1-2 years) to changes",
      "there_aren_t_clean_answers_some_people": "There aren't clean answers. Some people who eat fish + chicken decline octopus specifically. Some celebrity chefs (Dan Barber, Alice Waters) have stopped serving octopus. Some traditional cuisines argue this is colonial moralizing against ancient food practices. The ethics are genuinely contested + the conversation is genuinely open. This module doesn't take a position. The question is worth holding rather than resolving.",
      "there_aren_t_clean_answers_the_questio": "There aren't clean answers. The questions are genuinely open. That's what makes them worth thinking about.",
      "there_s_no_apex_cephalopod_even_the_la": "There's no \"apex cephalopod\" — even the largest face predators. Giant Pacific octopuses are eaten by harbor seals, sea otters, lingcod, and sometimes by other (larger) giant Pacific octopuses. Giant squid + colossal squid are sperm whale prey — and the whale carries the scars to prove it.",
      "there_s_no_scalar_smartness_axis": "There's no scalar \"smartness\" axis.",
      "these_are_real_research_priorities_ide": "These are real research priorities identified by the cephalopod biology community for the coming decade. Some of them may be the questions your students will help answer — directly or by laying the groundwork.",
      "these_discoveries_demonstrate_that_cep": "These discoveries demonstrate that cephalopod biology is NOT a closed book. Each year, new findings reshape our understanding of cephalopod cognition, sensory systems, evolution, and welfare implications. Citizen science contributions + AI-assisted analysis + new imaging technologies are expanding what's possible.",
      "these_same_questions_apply_to_the_huma": "These same questions apply to the human gut microbiome, plant-rhizobia nitrogen-fixing symbiosis, coral-algae bleaching dynamics, and probiotics research. The bobtail squid + Vibrio fischeri system is small enough to fully control + complex enough to be informative.",
      "they_are_apex_predators_with_no_natura": "They are apex predators with no natural enemies",
