      "butt_img": "Butt joint: two plates meeting edge to edge in the same plane, welded along the seam",
      "ch1_img": "Weld symbol: a horizontal reference line with a leader angling down to an arrowhead. A triangle sits below the reference line, with the text 1/4 to its left",
      "ch2_img": "Weld symbol: a horizontal reference line with a leader angling down to an arrowhead. An open circle marks the point where they meet and a small flag flies from it. A triangle sits below the reference line, with the text 3/16 to its left",
      "ch3_img": "Weld symbol: a horizontal reference line with a leader angling down to an arrowhead. A V opens below the reference line and a mirrored V opens above it, each marked 3/8",
      "ch4_img": "Weld symbol: a horizontal reference line with a leader angling down to an arrowhead and an open circle where they meet. Below the line is a V with a curve bulging downward beneath it, marked 1/2. The right end forks into a tail carrying the text GTAW-6G",
      "corner_img": "Corner joint: two plates meeting at an outside corner, welded along the outer seam",
      "edge_img": "Edge joint: two plates face to face with edges aligned, welded along the top edge",
      "lap_img": "Lap joint: one plate overlapping another, welded along the overlapping edge",
      "tee_img": "T-joint: a vertical plate meeting a horizontal plate at a right angle, welded where they meet",
      "0_024_thin_sheet_metal_autobody_22_ga_": "0.024\" — thin sheet metal (autobody, 22 ga). 0.030\" — light gauge (16-12 ga). 0.035\" — most common general work (1/8\"-3/8\"). 0.045\" — heavy plate (3/8\"+) + production work. Bigger wire = more amperage required = more deposition rate but less control.",
      "0_8_zirconiated_ewzr_1": "0.8% Zirconiated (EWZr-1)",
      "0_ft": "0 ft",
      "100_ft": "100 ft",
      "10_25_on_top_of_cost_basis_the_this_is": "10-25% on top of cost basis. The \"this is worth doing\" number.",
      "10_defects_identify_the_root_cause": "10 defects — identify the root cause",
      "10_real_world_welding_scenarios_for_ea": "10 real-world welding scenarios. For each, pick the correct process from MIG / TIG / Stick / FCAW / Resistance. Vignettes target the canonical decisions: stainless food-service, structural outdoor in wind, aluminum boat hull, sanitary brewery pipe, cast-iron engine block crack, automotive sheet metal, agricultural repair on rusty steel.",
      "10_vignettes_pick_the_right_process": "10 vignettes — pick the right process",
      "10_weld_defects_identify_the_root_caus": "10 weld defects — identify the root cause",
      "10_welding_scenarios_pick_the_right_pr": "10 welding scenarios — pick the right process",
      "12_narrative_profiles_of_working_welde": "12 narrative profiles of working welders: shipyard journeyman, pipeline traveler, nuclear specialist, ironworker, female pipefitter, artist welder, welding instructor, mining welder, motorcycle frame builder, race car fabricator, sculptor, marine welder. What they actually do, what they earn, what they wish they'd known, how they got there.",
      "12_real_welder_profiles_paths": "12 real welder profiles + paths",
      "150_multiple_choice_questions_welding_": "150 multiple-choice questions. Welding processes, metallurgy, weld design, distortion + residual stress, weld + base metal discontinuities, destructive + non-destructive examination, joint design, welding symbols, basic codes + standards. Open book — bring AWS reference materials.",
      "1_10_000_sec_or_faster_older_budget_he": "1/10,000 sec or faster. Older budget helmets at 1/3,600 sec — slow enough to flash your eyes. Spend the money.",
      "1_5_lanthanated_ewla_1_5": "1.5% Lanthanated (EWLa-1.5)",
      "1_always_use_local_exhaust_ventilation": "1. ALWAYS use local exhaust ventilation (LEV) on every weld, not just stainless. 2. Wear hearing protection on the shop floor, not just when grinding. 3. Take micro-breaks every 30-60 min for posture reset. 4. Get a doctor who knows occupational medicine; do annual spirometry. 5. Know your OSHA right to a clean shop + report violations without retaliation.",
      "1_anatomy_of_a_symbol": "1. Anatomy of a Symbol",
      "1_buy_the_aws_wi_manual_online_self_as": "1. Buy the AWS WI Manual + Online Self-Assessment ($150). Take + review repeatedly.",
      "1_coil_generates_alternating_magnetic_": "1. Coil generates alternating magnetic field near surface of conductive material.",
      "1_confined_space_permit_2_atmospheric_": "(1) Confined space permit, (2) atmospheric testing, (3) forced ventilation, (4) standby attendant outside with rescue equipment, (5) communication (radio or signal rope), (6) NEVER alone, (7) machine ON/OFF accessible from outside.",
      "1_fusion_zone_fz": "1. Fusion zone (FZ): ",
      "1_gear_up": "1. Gear Up",
      "1_reference_line": "1. Reference line: ",
      "1_revision_letter_matches_bom_work_ord": "1. ✓ Revision letter matches BOM + work order",
      "1_source_capture_lev": "1. Source capture LEV: ",
      "1_torch_is_mounted_in_a_weld_head_smal": "1. Torch is mounted in a \"weld head\" — small machine that clamps around the pipe + has a track that the torch travels along.",
      "1_transducer_piezoelectric_crystal_pre": "1. Transducer (piezoelectric crystal) pressed against surface with couplant gel.",
      "1_why_welding": "1. Why Welding",
      "200_ft": "200 ft",
      "24_000_0_020_0_000_24_000_to_24_020_20": "\"24.000 +0.020/-0.000\" = 24.000 to 24.020 (20 thou window, only positive allowed).",
      "24_000_0_030_23_970_to_24_030_60_thou_": "\"24.000 ± 0.030\" = 23.970 to 24.030 (60 thou window).",
      "24_7_with_only_routine_maintenance_bre": "24/7 with only routine maintenance breaks.",
      "2_4_welders_add_fill_passes_simultaneo": "2-4 welders add fill passes simultaneously (different sides of the joint). Speed is critical — pipeline construction is paid per foot of pipe laid.",
      "2_5x_faster_than_skilled_manual_welder": "2-5x faster than skilled manual welder for repeating same joint.",
